//! WavPack decoding (`.wv`): lossless and hybrid-lossy integer audio, mono, stereo and
//! multichannel, with the 32-bit extension stream.
//!
//! The layout comes from David Bryant's "WavPack 4 & 5 Binary File / Block Format" (kept in
//! `docs/specs`). The entropy coder and the decorrelation passes follow his BSD-licensed
//! reference decoder, which is the only complete description of them; its notice is reproduced
//! in `docs/formats/wavpack.md`. The two logarithm tables are generated by formula (checked
//! against the reference's tables) instead of copied.
//!
//! Not supported: floating-point blocks, DSD blocks, correction (`.wvc`) files.
use crate::{ape, check_samples, Audio, Samples};
